    "['local-address [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'router bgp 100', 'parent_command': ['router bgp 100'], 'root': 'router bgp 100', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the given Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 100\\nneighbor 10.3.1.1 update-source 10.3.1.2\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper command specifies the local address (source IP) to use for BGP peering with AS 100\\n- In Cisco, this is achieved using the `update-source` parameter under the BGP neighbor configuration\\n- The AS number (100) is derived from the group name \"remote-as-100\" in the original configuration\\n- The neighbor IP (10.3.1.1) comes from the corresponding neighbor statement in the Juniper config', 'trans_template': 'router bgp 100'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 10.3.1.1 update-source 10.3.1.2', 'parent_command': ['router bgp 100'], 'root': 'router bgp 100', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the given Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 100\\nneighbor 10.3.1.1 update-source 10.3.1.2\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper command specifies the local address (source IP) to use for BGP peering with AS 100\\n- In Cisco, this is achieved using the `update-source` parameter under the BGP neighbor configuration\\n- The AS number (100) is derived from the group name \"remote-as-100\" in the original configuration\\n- The neighbor IP (10.3.1.1) comes from the corresponding neighbor statement in the Juniper config', 'trans_template': 'neighbor 10.3.1.1 update-source 10.3.1.2'}]]": 1,
